      "knowledge_point": "Finding the Asymptotes of a Vertical Hyperbola Given in Standard Form",
      "problem": "Find the asymptotes of the hyperbola $\\frac{{y}^{2}}{64}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}=1.$",
      "worked_solution": "The standard equation of a vertical hyperbola centered at the origin is\n\n$$\n\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\nFor a vertical hyperbola centered at the origin, the equations of the asymptotes are\n\n$$\ny=\\pm \\frac{a}{b}x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have \n\n$$\na=\\sqrt{64}=8,\\,b=\\sqrt{4}=2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the asymptotes of the hyperbola are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\pm \\frac{8}{2}x \\\\  & =\\pm 4x.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
